            {
                id repair.tests-root
                title "Restore root integration test targets"
                priority 0
                kind @test
                deps (repair.tests-cfg)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:21:00.786787Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:52:42.280642Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Suite restored: 457 tests run / 457 passed / 2 skipped against live Postgres 16 (Docker). Deleted files: connection_tests (API gone), stream_tests (streaming removed by design), time_crate_tests (time support removed; time dev-dep dropped). Deleted in-src mock-layer test modules (loader/select consolidation, update RecordNotUpdated, MockRow) — coverage now lives in the live integration suite. Behavior changes verified spec-consistent: UpdateOne zero-row -> RecordNotFound; select_only over an omitted Option column errors; into_json removed. macros.derive.test-attr rule bumped to +1 (kill-switch cfg removed from the expansion). Ignored pending fixes: sql_err classifier (not implemented), bits save_as BIT(8) (ValueHolder ToSql ignores inferred wire types). Escalations for follow-up nodes: ValueHolder parameter typing (BIT + int-vs-float8 wire errors), no explicit DatabaseTransaction::rollback, no unprepared/batch execution reachable, dead private begin_with_config (isolation levels unreachable), pool-level parallelism untestable, doctests broadly broken (~224 lines referencing removed API), insert select_as-in-RETURNING cast coverage gap."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:52:56.738375Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id repair.tests-crates
                title "Fix pgorm-pool and pgorm-macros test targets"
                priority 0
                kind @test
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T19:40:54.065149Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T19:40:56.784229Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Scope addition: pgorm-codegen's test target is broken in the same API-drift class (transformer.rs cfg(test) imports pgorm::DbBackend and calls the old Schema::new(backend) signature) — folded into this node alongside pgorm-pool and pgorm-macros."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:00:48.1169Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Two substantive calls made while restoring the targets: (1) DeriveValueType was genuinely regressed — commit 6177d6b5 added a Display bound to TryGetable::try_get_by and missed the derive's emitted impl, so the macro could not compile for any input; fixed the macro (pgorm-macros/src/derives/value_type.rs), not the test. (2) The four transformer golden-fixture tests failed because an inherited upstream commit (27af2c9c) rustfmt-normalized token-level fixture details; restored the fixtures' byte-exact forms in pgorm's own files and put #[rustfmt::skip] on their module decls so the fmt commit-gate cannot re-corrupt them. Also removed pgorm-pool's dead cfg(feature=\"serde\") test gate (serde is unconditional there) and added with-rust_decimal to pgorm-codegen's dev-dep — noting latent rot: cargo check -p pgorm --no-default-features --features macros fails (cursor.rs Decimal ToSql needs with-rust_decimal)."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:00:52.916149Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id repair.cursor-tosql
                title "Remove u8/u16 unsigned types; implement Vector/IpNetwork/MacAddress cursor binding"
                priority 0
                kind @fix
                deps (repair.tests-root)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T19:31:53.79001Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Operator decision: remove TinyUnsigned (u8) and SmallUnsigned (u16) support end-to-end instead of implementing ToSql widening — Postgres has no unsigned integer types, so the variants are MySQL-era dead vocabulary; deleting them turns the cursor-binding runtime panic into a compile error. Unsigned (u32) stays: it has a real Postgres meaning (oid). BigUnsigned (u64) to be assessed during implementation. Vector/IpNetwork/MacAddress todo!() arms still get real bindings."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T20:54:08.743144Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T21:16:41.139539Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Implementation outcomes: u8/u16 removed end-to-end (compile error confirmed via macro probe); u32 kept (oid); u64/BigUnsigned KEPT — live use found: every LIMIT/OFFSET binds Value::BigUnsigned (write-only, no decode needed). Vector binds via pgvector's postgres feature; IpNetwork/MacAddress hand-encoded with postgres_protocol::types::{inet_to_sql,macaddr_to_sql} (new root dep postgres-protocol, already in the lockfile via tokio-postgres; ipnetwork/mac_address ship no ToSql and the orphan rule forbids one here; IpAddr delegation rejected — would silently drop the prefix on writes). 9 spec rules bumped to +1 with all sites re-pinned. Follow-up gaps queued: no decode (TryGetable) for Vector/IpNetwork/MacAddress; payload types not re-exported; accepts()-always-true type mismatch (bits_tests stays ignored); pgorm-migration/src/schema.rs still references deleted unsigned builders (uncompiled module, prune at decide.migration)."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-01T21:16:54.2968Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

