                title "WINDOW clause renders after ORDER BY/LIMIT/locking; PG requires it before ORDER BY"
                deps (bug.char-render)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T12:33:46.917044Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit: prepare_select_statement writes ORDER BY (query_builder.rs:262), LIMIT/OFFSET (:273), locking (:275), THEN the named WINDOW clause (:280). PostgreSQL grammar places WINDOW between HAVING and ORDER BY, so window() combined with any of those renders a syntax error; existing tests only exercise window in isolation. Plain rendering-order fix; bumps sql.render.window (and check sql.render.select-order's clause-order claim). Add a combined window+order_by+limit test."
                    }

