                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Oracle expansion of scope: the position fix alone is not enough. (1) Named windows render without parentheses — WINDOW \"w\" AS PARTITION BY ... is invalid even in isolation; PG requires WINDOW \"w\" AS (PARTITION BY ...). (2) The six window_* tests all render unparseable SQL for a second reason: OVER is being attached to a bare column expression in projection contexts where PG rejects it — read oracle_pins_window_clause_parens and the assert_eq_unparsed! sites in window.rs (12 marked) for the full picture. Fix all three defects together and flip the pins + the 12 unparsed markers to oracle-checked assertions. sql.render.window and possibly sql.ast.window-statement bump."
                    }

