            {
                id bug.test-harness
                title "Test harness swallows CREATE DATABASE failures and races teardown under parallelism"
                kind @test
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T16:56:52.912497Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Diagnosed by the char-render agent after a one-in-four flake: tests/common/setup/mod.rs:30 discards the CREATE DATABASE result (let _create_db_result = ...), so under parallel contention the create can fail silently and the test connects to an unprovisioned database (observed: active_enum_tests main failing then passing in isolation). Related but distinct: the DROP DATABASE ... WITH (FORCE) teardown kills peer connections at high nextest parallelism (the recurring 57P01 \"terminating connection due to administrator command\" flakes that forced -j 4). Fix both: propagate the create result (retry-once on the known contention error if needed), and make teardown not shoot peers — or serialize creates/drops through an advisory lock on the maintenance connection. Goal: full-parallelism nextest runs stop flaking and the -j 4 crutch can go."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T18:15:49.653955Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Scope addition: pgorm-macros/tests/compile-fail/value_type_lifetime_field.stderr is churn-fragile — it snapshots an E0277 whose bound list re-renders on every ValueType/IntoIdentity trait-surface change (re-blessed three times in one campaign; also the source of the false \"pre-existing failure\" reports from worktree agents whose stale expected-files diverged). The lifetime-rejection contract is already pinned by the churn-proof unit tests in sql_type_match.rs (macro-spans added them for exactly this reason). When working this node, decide: delete the fragile fixture in favor of the unit pins, or keep it and accept the re-bless ritual."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T18:41:30.181606Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Operator directive: agents must not mass create/drop against the shared server, and the primary flake mechanism is now understood to be CROSS-WORKTREE collision — concurrent agents run the same test binaries, per-test database names derive solely from the test fn name, so two runs share one database and one's DROP ... WITH (FORCE) kills the other's connections (57P01) or races its CREATE. The fix is worktree/process-unique database names (suffix a short hash of the checkout path or pid into TestContext's derivation) plus propagating the CREATE result. Campaign protocol adjusted: agents run scoped DB tests only; the lead runs the full suite serially at integration."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T19:15:03.593799Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }
        )
