            {
                id pgparse.fingerprint
                title "Query fingerprinting for the metrics layer via pg_query normalize/fingerprint"
                deps (pgparse.oracle)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-02T14:49:19.695888Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "pg_query::fingerprint gives stable constants-normalized query identities (the shape pg_stat_statements thinks in) and normalize gives the $n-parameterized text. Wire into the opt-in metrics layer: the instrumented wrappers tag statement hooks with the fingerprint so a MetricsCollector can aggregate by query shape instead of raw SQL text. Design questions at start: where the fingerprint is computed (per-call vs memoized by statement text — a small cache matters since the hot path repeats statements), and whether MetricsCollector grows a parameter (breaking the trait — it has no default methods by design, metric.layer.collector bumps) or the fingerprint rides in an existing argument. Runtime dependency on pg_query gated behind a feature on pgorm even with the tax waived — the metrics layer's whole design is unwrapped-code-pays-nothing (metric.layer rule). Deps on pgparse.oracle for plumbing/version pin."
                    }

