                        text "Entities from a schema.sql with no live database: parse CREATE TABLE (and CREATE TYPE ... AS ENUM, CREATE INDEX, COMMENT ON) via pg_query, bridge the PG parse tree into pgorm-query's TableCreateStatement/TypeCreateStatement, and feed the existing EntityTransformer pipeline. Scope decision at start: the supported DDL subset (start with what the transformer consumes — columns, types, PK/unique/FK constraints, enums; reject the rest with named TransformErrors, never silently drop — the Turso COMPAT.md's \"silently ignored\" pattern is the anti-goal). Deps on nopanic.codegen-gate (build on the fallible transform surface, avoid churn collision in pgorm-codegen) and pgparse.oracle (plumbing). New spec rules under codegen.; the bridge is also reusable groundwork if migration diffing ever becomes a want."
